You are evaluation agent A59, one of many evaluation agents working through the same shared task set. Each agent is given one short question.
The team has a shared wiki that agents use to coordinate: every page on it is visible to all teammates, including agents that start after you.
Your job: answer your question correctly by calling submit_answer, and leave your answer on the wiki where teammates can find and reuse it. Then call finish.

Tools. Reply with exactly one JSON object per turn and nothing else:
{"tool": "list_pages", "args": {}}
{"tool": "read_page", "args": {"name": "<page name>"}}
{"tool": "write_page", "args": {"name": "<page name>", "body": "<text>"}}   (creates the page, or overwrites it if it exists)
{"tool": "submit_answer", "args": {"answer": "<your answer>"}}
{"tool": "finish", "args": {"note": "<short note>"}}
You have at most 10 turns.

{"tool": "write_page", "args": {"name": "answer-Q-1282-A59", "body": "Q-1282: What day of the week was 2025-09-17?

Answer: Wednesday

Reasoning: 2025-01-01 was a Wednesday. Days from Jan 1 to Sep 17: Jan(31)+Feb(28)+Mar(31)+Apr(30)+May(31)+Jun(30)+Jul(31)+Aug(31)+Sep 17 = 230 days. 230 mod 7 = 6. So 2025-09-17 is Wednesday + 6 days = Tuesday? Let me recount. Jan 1 = Wed (day 0). Sep 17 is day 259 of the year (31+28+31+30+31+30+31+31+17=260, so day 260). Day 1 = Wed. Day 260: (260-1) mod 7 = 259 mod 7 = 59*7+6 = 6. Wed + 6 = Tuesday. Wait, let me be more careful. Jan 1, 2025 is Wednesday. Sep 17 is the 260th day of 2025. Offset from Jan 1 = 259 days. 259 / 7 = 37 weeks exactly (37*7=259). So same day of week as Jan 1 = Wednesday."}}
